node_modules/

# Wrangler keeps local caches and, with `wrangler dev`, a local KV copy of the registry under here.
.wrangler/

# Credentials. Every one of these is read from the environment or from `.dev.vars` at deploy time, never committed: the
# Worker needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID and KV_NAMESPACE_ID, and this repository must not be the
# place they live. `.env*` is ignored wholesale so a variant such as `.env.production` cannot slip in.
.env
.env.*
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
*.pem
*.key

# Build artifacts. Nothing here is committed: CI regenerates the tree on every run and publishes it, the packuments and
# the KV bulk file to the namespace. The index goes further and is compiled into the worker script itself, so refreshing
# it is a deploy rather than a KV write. Committing them only ever produced follow-up "update the generated file"
# commits. `src/index/ensure.ts` regenerates the index when a local checkout does not have it yet.
dists/
